{title: 131 Bendito es el nombre de Jesús}
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{lyricist: William W. How (1823-1897); Vers. esp.: Tulio N. Peverini (1932-}
{composer: Ralph Vaughan Williams (1872-1958)}

{sov}
1.
[F]Ben[Bb]dito [C]es [Dm]el [Bb]nom[F]bre [Gm]de [C]Je[F]sús,
[C]a [G]cuantos [C]le [F]confiesan [G]con [C]amor.
[F]Jesús es Rey [C]por [F]la [C]eternidad,
¡A[F]le[Bb]lu[Dm]ya! [F]¡A[Gm]le[F]lu[C]ya![F]
{eov}

{sov}
2.
[F]Tú [Bb]eres [C]Se[Dm]ñor, [Bb]Cas[F]tillo [Gm]y [C]Ro[F]ca fiel;
[C]el [G]Capi[C]tán [F]que lucha [G]contra [C]el mal;
[F]bendita Luz [C]en [F]la [C]oscuridad,
¡A[F]le[Bb]lu[Dm]ya! [F]¡A[Gm]le[F]lu[C]ya![F]
{eov}

{sov}
3.
[F]Que [Bb]con [C]va[Dm]lor [Bb]pe[F]leen [Gm]por [C]Je[F]sús
[C]los [G]santos [C]que [F]aman a [G]su [C]Salvador.
[F]Dios les dará, [C]por [F]gra[C]cia, galardón,
¡A[F]le[Bb]lu[Dm]ya! [F]¡A[Gm]le[F]lu[C]ya![F]
{eov}

{sov}
4.
[F]De [Bb]mar [C]a [Dm]mar [Bb]y [F]en la [Gm]San[C]ta [F]Ciudad,
[C]el [G]canto [C]pron[F]to habrá [G]de [C]resonar
[F]al Creador, [C]ben[F]dito [C]Redentor:
¡A[F]le[Bb]lu[Dm]ya! [F]¡A[Gm]le[F]lu[C]ya![F]
{eov}
